# Environment variables — URAL Travel Intelligence
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: this project does NOT read a `.env` file at build time.
#
# The site is a static Vite build (Cloudflare Pages) with one serverless
# function: `functions/api/subscribe.js`. Those variables are read at REQUEST
# time from the Pages runtime, so they must be set in the Cloudflare Pages
# dashboard, not locally:
#
#   Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages → ural-travel → Settings
#   → Variables and Secrets → add → type "Secret" → Save
#
# This file is a checklist of what to set there. Nothing here is loaded
# automatically, and nothing here should ever contain a real key.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# RESEND_API_KEY — REQUIRED for the contact form and newsletter signups.
#
# Both `/api/contact` and `/api/subscribe` deliver through the Resend API from
# the verified `uraltravel.co.uk` domain. This is now the ONLY transport: the
# FormSubmit relay was removed on 2026-10-25 (see
# docs/growth/20-FORM-AND-MAIL-HARDENING-2026-10-25.md).
#
# Without this secret the endpoints answer `503 mail_transport_not_configured`
# instead of pretending to succeed. There is no silent fallback by design: a
# second relay meant a second processor saw every visitor's name and phone.
#
# Where to set it: Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages → ural-travel →
# Settings → Variables and Secrets → add → type "Secret" → Save.
# Where to get it: https://resend.com → API Keys → Create API Key (`re_…`).
#
# ⚠️ Never commit the real value. If it has ever been committed, pasting it into
#    a chat, a screenshot, an issue or a commit message counts as leaked —
#    rotate it in the Resend dashboard. Deleting the file does NOT remove it from
#    git history, and this repository is public.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"


# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY — optional, but recommended. Enables bot verification on
# `/api/contact` via Cloudflare Turnstile.
#
# ⚠️ DEPLOYMENT ORDER MATTERS. The server only enforces Turnstile when this
#    secret exists. The widget only renders when the PUBLIC site key below was
#    present at build time. If you set this secret without rebuilding with the
#    site key, every visitor is rejected with `403 turnstile_failed`.
#    Correct order: set `VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` as a *build* variable first,
#    deploy, then add this secret.
#
# Where to get it: Cloudflare dashboard → Turnstile → your widget → Secret Key.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY="0x4AAAAAAA..."

# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY — optional; the PUBLIC site key for the same widget.
# Read at BUILD time by Vite, so it belongs in Cloudflare Pages → Settings →
# Environment variables (Production + Preview), not in the Functions secrets.
# Absent = no widget, no token, and the server skips verification.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="0x4AAAAAAA..."

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Removed 2026-10-13 — AI Studio scaffold leftovers that this project never used.
#
# These documented `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL`. Neither is read anywhere in
# the repository; the site calls no Gemini API and has no OAuth callback. They
# described a different runtime and misled anyone setting up a deployment.
# See docs/history/ for the consolidation record.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
